{"id": "EUVD-2026-108835", "enisaUuid": "afefc373-8f2c-3ca8-a9bb-6022a81dcc04", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKEYS: Fix add_key() race with keyring restriction\n\n__key_create_or_update() snapshots keyring->restrict_link before taking\nthe destination keyring's semaphore.  keyring_restrict() installs a\nrestriction while holding that semaphore.\n\nThis allows a writer to observe no restriction, wait for the keyring\nowner to install a reject-all restriction and return successfully, and\nthen link a key using the stale NULL snapshot.  The writer only needs\nwrite permission on the destination keyring.\n\nMove the restrict_link read after __key_link_lock() and\n__key_link_begin().  The read and the subsequent restriction check are\nthen serialized with restriction installation by keyring->sem.\n\nThe race was reproduced on v7.2.8 in 19 executions where restriction\ninstallation returned before the link completed.  All 19 linked the key\ndespite the reject-all restriction.  With this change, 312 executions\nreached the same ordering and every add_key() call failed with -EPERM.\n\nThe issue was found by manual concurrency analysis assisted by AI-based\nanalysis and independently verified with a QEMU reproducer and kernel\ninstrumentation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:21:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:21:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/305f1828b871dd46bf41addeb6f11d2c162dcb25", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f99399b48e3edd6851fac34cd329bab9f1f33baf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11516a0c402a6c1fa52254aa70d8d65fb921e59e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da0b595d8e6e2dd798f6e34e09dc51a13b888514", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd3ea3fcba7c75493760cdbccd35f029597e8d5e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99040"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20058cad-e8d0-3328-8d74-afa6cd56434c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.7"}, {"id": "3f9b0af8-a162-336f-b85c-e374b7547d63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac7eace2d00eab5ae0e9fdee63e38aee6001f7c <dd3ea3fcba7c75493760cdbccd35f029597e8d5e"}, {"id": "4aff903e-be93-32a5-917d-3d5a2844f86f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "5b331f74-7c3c-35c2-98ef-7e738987bb39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac7eace2d00eab5ae0e9fdee63e38aee6001f7c <f99399b48e3edd6851fac34cd329bab9f1f33baf"}, {"id": "84572d8a-5b4a-3ba3-b25b-19c3ade92bda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a98fe999-5755-3b01-8d5e-ca2c0713bb87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "babf3166-f1a0-3ae2-856a-5dab837c0400", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "c6443a8f-2ae2-3f79-a1c2-19f22263d0a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac7eace2d00eab5ae0e9fdee63e38aee6001f7c <11516a0c402a6c1fa52254aa70d8d65fb921e59e"}, {"id": "c7d5bd61-e5b5-36dd-8ab1-8add8d4f2582", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac7eace2d00eab5ae0e9fdee63e38aee6001f7c <305f1828b871dd46bf41addeb6f11d2c162dcb25"}, {"id": "f1076888-f243-3b1e-9f41-fe6179808f6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ac7eace2d00eab5ae0e9fdee63e38aee6001f7c <da0b595d8e6e2dd798f6e34e09dc51a13b888514"}, {"id": "f9a069bd-4fdc-3557-bef7-d3a9958eb190", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "fc86c957-c193-32f9-971f-7cedf41435a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "716f989f-6d7f-33e5-9c5c-eacf4988b6c0